{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nRelation-scoped unlink was added to the core, public library, and CLI, and MCP parity is tracked by airy-starchy-muntjac. Two maintained documentation surfaces still state the pre-change contract: `docs/ticket-model.md` says `unlink <source> <target>` takes no relation argument, and `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt` says unlink has no relation arg. This contradicts the current optional relation accepted by `rebar.unlink` and `rebar unlink`. The Phase 1 sibling sweep also found the same obsolete operation wording in `docs/event-schema.md`; its event-shape description must distinguish the relation selector from the emitted link-UUID cancellation.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a held-out contract test through the real packaged top-level CLI help and maintained public documentation surfaces.\n- Update the ticket-model and packaged overview surfaces to document `unlink <source> <target> [relation]`.\n- Preserve and explain the omitted-relation most-recent fallback.\n- State that an explicit canonical relation removes exactly that relation while preserving other active relations on the pair.\n- Correct the event-schema operation wording while preserving the true event payload semantics.\n- Regenerate any derived guide/reference output if these sources feed one.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The ticket-model unlink section documents the optional relation argument.\n- [ ] The packaged CLI overview documents the optional relation argument through real `rebar --help` output.\n- [ ] Both surfaces preserve the omitted-selector most-recent fallback contract.\n- [ ] Both surfaces describe exact relation-scoped removal.\n- [ ] The event schema distinguishes optional operation selection from UUID-targeted UNLINK event cancellation.\n- [ ] Documentation drift and relevant help tests pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787089575574840001,"uuid":"986180ef-fc50-4262-9f3f-f8be9cdc6b77"}